<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Rotary Dimension Allocation Details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report the exact number of hidden dimensions to which RoPE is applied for each configuration.
Because RoPE rotates hidden states in pairs, the number of rotated dimensions must be even.
Accordingly, percentage-based specifications are rounded to the nearest valid even number of dimensions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This adjustment only occurs for <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pythia</span>, which has a head dimension of 256. A nominal 10% corresponds
to 25.6 dimensions and would be rounded to 25 by the training framework. Since RoPE requires pairwise
rotation, we instead use 26 dimensions (10.2%) to ensure a valid pair count.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting rotated dimensions for each model are listed in Tables <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix A Rotary Dimension Allocation Details ‣ Fractional Rotation, Full Potential?Investigating Performance and Convergence of Partial RoPE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
